        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1852 Democratic National Convention\n- People: Franklin Pierce, Lewis Cass, James Buchanan, Stephen A. Douglas, Andrew Jackson\n- Places: Michigan, Pennsylvania, Illinois\n- Roles: President, United States Senator, Cabinet member, military officer, politician, statesman\n\nFacts:\n- Lewis Cass was the Democratic presidential nominee in 1848.\n- On the 49th ballot, the 1852 Democratic National Convention nominated Franklin Pierce for President as a dark horse candidate.\n- The 1852 Democratic National Convention passed over Lewis Cass of Michigan, James Buchanan of Pennsylvania, and Stephen A. Douglas of Illinois.\n- Lewis Cass lived from October 9, 1782, to June 17, 1866.\n- Lewis Cass was an American military officer, politician, and statesman.\n- Lewis Cass represented Michigan in the United States Senate.\n- Lewis Cass served in the Cabinets of Andrew Jackson and James Buchanan.",
